Rule 1 (x and y must have the same supported integer dtype)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= (1 ≤ dtype_(v_1) ∧ dtype_(v_1) ≤ 5) ∧ dtype_(v_1) = dtype_(v_2)
>>
Rule 2 (x and y must be broadcast-compatible)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (ndim(v_1) = 0 ∧ ndim(v_2) = 0) then true else ∀i ∈ [0, if ndim(v_1) ≥ ndim(v_2) then ndim(v_1) - 1 else ndim(v_2) - 1] : (ndim(v_1) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ (ndim(v_2) - i - 1 < 0) ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1) = 1 ∨ shape(v_1, ndim(v_1) - i - 1) = shape(v_2, ndim(v_2) - i - 1)
>>
Rule 3 (shift amounts must be non-negative and less than the bit-width of x)
{v_1 : tensor, v_2 : tensor} |= if (dtype_(v_1) = 1 ∨ dtype_(v_1) = 5) then (min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ 7) else if dtype_(v_1) = 2 then (min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ 15) else if dtype_(v_1) = 3 then (min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ 31) else if dtype_(v_1) = 4 then (min(v_2) ≥ 0 ∧ max(v_2) ≤ 63) else false
